  "result": "I fixed all three problems, but I haven't run the test suite or any other check.\n\n1. **Switching off doesn't stick:** `updateEndpoint` in `src/server/repositories/webhook-repository.ts` only wrote `enabled` when it was truthy, so `false` was dropped. It now writes whenever `enabled` is given, so switching an endpoint off and back on both save. The queueing code already skipped switched-off endpoints, so no new deliveries are queued once the flag is saved.\n2. **Queued deliveries for a switched-off endpoint:** `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts` now marks a delivery failed and counts it in `failed` when its endpoint is switched off, the same way it already did for a missing endpoint. Deliveries for endpoints that are still on go out as before.\n3. **Endpoint allowance:** `createWebhook` in `src/server/services/webhook-service.ts` now counts every endpoint, on or off, against the plan limit, so switching one off no longer lets a workspace create another.",
